id: pm-github-uqjf
title: Require explicit delivery attribution before merged-PR closeout
description: "pm-ado issue 33 shows that PR 16 reported a statement-coverage gap while PR 19 delivered it using a structured PM item: declaration. Require PR-body delivery declarations, reject mentions and tracker PR URL metadata alone, and select the latest eligible merged declaration with consistent durable evidence."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[1]: changelog-unreleased
created_at: "2026-10-18T18:19:06.214Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T20:40:50.443Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[41]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T18:21:36.252Z",codex-agent,"Root cause confirmed: in_progress bypasses delivery declarations, and ascending PR selection chooses the earlier gap-reporting PR. https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/issues/33 compares https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/pull/16 with https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/pull/19. Neither body declares closure, so both must be reported without closing unless a canonical item-to-PR link supplies delivery evidence. A separate fix/closeout-explicit-delivery PR will retain all prior history."
  "2026-10-18T18:27:43.386Z",codex-agent,"Implemented explicit delivery declarations (closing canonical links, whole-line closing item ids or pm-github trailers, and exact PR URL metadata). The full selection is resolved before SDK writes; competing merged delivery claims receive ambiguous_delivery. Added minimal public title/body/commit fixtures from real pm-ado PRs 16 and 19. The real bodies contain only mentions; both are now refused until delivery is explicitly linked. Updated previous positive fixtures to declare delivery instead of relying on status."
  "2026-10-18T18:30:07.355Z",codex-agent,"Function-only behavioral revert: restored the old in_progress bypass in runCloseout while retaining both real-shape regression tests. Both tests fail: the earlier gap-reporting PR is accepted and the explicit PR 19 selection loses provenance. Restoring explicit attribution makes the linked four-case suite pass, including ambiguous-claim refusal and whole-line declarations. The package pins, source inventory and 100 percent thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-18T18:48:06.831Z",codex-agent,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/150 is open at 69ab7dec54bd1493e632d98dab5aa3b7f09a4fee. Fresh --no-local clone strict health passes with required merge drivers in an isolated home. The current full npm gate passes all 4 new real-shape attribution cases, including the additional foreign/unknown canonical-link boundary. Current-head function-only revert copies are being rechecked without mutating any running gate checkout. CodeQL and Semgrep pass; full runtime gates and Node 22/26 CI are still running."
  "2026-10-18T18:54:50.388Z",codex-agent,"CI Node 26 passed 897/897 tests with zero failures, skips or cancellations, then the unchanged exact branch gate correctly refused 99.96 percent. closeout.ts line 490 lacked the compact-report positive-close arm after former multi-PR success fixtures became ambiguity refusals. Added an assertion that a real single-delivery dry-run remains close in compact output; no production code or threshold change. Superseded local closeout gates were stopped to rerun the complete corrected test corpus."
  "2026-10-18T18:57:14.608Z",codex-agent,"Focused compact projection verification passed: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"dry-run plans same-repo\" test/closeout.test.ts, 1/1 with zero failures/skips. This preserves a valid single-delivery close action alongside individual refusals and routine skip counts; the exact branch gate will rerun without weakening its threshold. Current-head real-shape function-only revert copies failed 2/2, with zero test-load failures."
  "2026-10-18T21:13:13.683Z",codex-agent,"Code-head CI is green at b21ff5bdbdcfdab6c97b1204d73ff528b0f65745: Node 22 and 26 passed with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage over 14 authored modules; Node 22 reports 897/897 tests with zero skips or failures. CodeQL and Semgrep passed. Full local npm and Bun release checks are still running; no local completion is claimed yet. Automated reviewer approval is missing: Sourcery quota, CodeRabbit skipped review, and Greptile ended trial. CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/39156538670."
  "2026-10-18T22:13:39.500Z",codex-agent,"Full local npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exited 0 at code head b21ff5bdbdcfdab6c97b1204d73ff528b0f65745. Each passed 897/897 tests with zero failures, skips or cancellations and exact 100/100/100/100 over all 14 authored modules: 10471 lines and statements, 274 functions and 3187 branches, all covered. Typecheck, build, docstrings, lint, duplication, privacy, production audit, pack dry run, changelog check and publication-attestation checks passed at unchanged pins and thresholds. The linked real-shape suite passed 4/4 and the compact single-delivery case passed 1/1; reverting only the old in-progress bypass makes both real-shape regressions fail. GitHub independently confirms delivery PR 19 merged at 2026-10-08T01:19:51Z. PR 150 is separate from release PR 149; existing pm-ado PR 32 records remain untouched and need regeneration with explicit PR 19 evidence. Final receipt checks and final-head CI follow. No merge, release dispatch, tag or publication was performed."
  "2026-10-18T22:54:00.823Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: new PR150 threads PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM6tvYM7 and PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM6tvYM- are confirmed. Whole-line delivery declarations currently accept newline whitespace between keyword and item id; ambiguity rewriting also changes mention-only rows when other PRs claim delivery. Restrict declarations to horizontal whitespace and rewrite only rows whose PR is in the existing claimant set. Extend real-SDK attribution scenarios with multiline negatives and two claimants plus a mention-only PR. Full npm/Bun gates and function-only revert proofs follow; threads remain unanswered and unresolved."
  "2026-10-18T22:55:26.292Z",codex-agent,"Review regressions pass 6/6 against real temporary SDK trackers. Function-only behavioral revert proofs: restoring only the old declaration regex in runCloseout makes the multiline-keyword/trailer scenario fail with ERR_ASSERTION (exit 1); removing only claimant PR membership from the ambiguity condition makes the two-claims-plus-mention scenario fail with ERR_ASSERTION (exit 1). Both retain current tests and other fixes. Same-line spaces/tabs, real linked PR19 chronology and single-delivery compact output remain covered. Typecheck, lint and docstrings pass. Full npm/Bun gates remain pending."
  "2026-10-18T23:32:52.582Z",codex-agent,"Review code-head CI is green at c9a29d199ac9982e842e28cfdf6b75fb014572c3: Node22 and Node26 each passed 899/899 Node tests, exact 100/100/100/100 over 14 authored modules, and 899 native Bun tests across 41 files. CodeQL and Semgrep passed; 60-second polling finished within 40 minutes. CI receipt: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/39174854340 . Both explicit local release checks remain in progress. Review threads have not been replied to or resolved."
  "2026-10-18T23:43:08.088Z",codex-agent,"The first concurrent Bun release-check attempt hit the existing startup-sensitive watchdog probe tracked by pm-github-sah1: test/bounded-cli.test.ts failed its /ready/ assertion because stdout was empty before the unchanged 500 ms child deadline. All six changed attribution scenarios passed in that attempt; both Node22/26 CI jobs passed all 899 tests and exact coverage. Stopped the already-failed execution (exit 143) to avoid spending resources on an invalid run; resulting cancellation diagnostics are not additional regressions. Isolated node --test test/bounded-cli.test.ts passes 2/2 unchanged. A complete Bun release-check rerun will run after the other local gates finish, with unchanged coverage thresholds, test/helper budgets and dependency pins. This reuses the existing follow-up instead of creating a duplicate."
  "2026-10-19T00:19:52.087Z",codex-agent,"The explicit npm run release:check completed with exit 0 at code head c9a29d199ac9982e842e28cfdf6b75fb014572c3: 899/899 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations, exact 100/100/100/100 over 14 authored modules. Lines/statements 10472/10472; functions 274/274; branches 3187/3187. All remaining release-check stages passed. The complete bun run release:check rerun has now started after the other local gates finished, with unchanged test/helper budgets, thresholds, source scope and dependency pins. Earlier interrupted concurrent Bun results remain documented separately; no final Bun completion is claimed yet."
  "2026-10-19T00:50:27.912Z",codex-agent,"The complete unchanged Bun rerun has passed the 500 ms startup-watchdog control and all six real-SDK attribution scenarios, including both new review regressions. Remaining workflow acceptance and coverage aggregation are still in progress; no full Bun completion is claimed. The companion release PR149 is now complete at 7b61575b5e1a29ed929358f188456412f6b3b769 with both 903-test local gates, final Node22/26 CI and independent fresh-clone strict health/validation/privacy: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/39179989399 . This attribution branch stays separately verified; combined merge acceptance remains with the orchestrator."
  "2026-10-19T01:20:55.272Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 full gates completed at code head c9a29d199ac9982e842e28cfdf6b75fb014572c3: npm run release:check and the complete bun run release:check rerun both exited 0. Each passed 899/899 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations and exact 100/100/100/100 over 14 authored modules. Lines/statements 10472/10472; functions 274/274; branches npm 3187/3187 and Bun invocation 3185/3185. All stages passed with unchanged thresholds, source scope, dependency pins and helper/test budgets. The initial concurrent Bun attempt reproduced existing pm-github-sah1 /ready/ startup sensitivity and was stopped; the unchanged full rerun passed the 500 ms watchdog as well as all tests. The follow-up remains open. Focused attribution suite 6/6 and compact control 1/1 passed. Restoring only the old declaration regex makes the multiline regression fail; removing only claimant membership makes the two-claimants-plus-mention regression fail, both with ERR_ASSERTION. Same-line/tab declarations, real linked PR19 chronology and mention-only row fidelity remain intact. Completed receipts and initial-flake disclosure are in docs/explicit-closeout-attribution.md. Code-head CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/39174854340 . Receipt-head CI and independent fresh-clone strict health follow in the PR. No review-thread replies/resolutions or release actions occurred."
  "2026-10-19T02:00:19.487Z",codex-agent,"Merge origin/main after PR 149 into PR 150 using the configured PM merge drivers. The only merge conflict is CHANGELOG.md; retain main's version and regenerate after tracker writes. Check clone-local receipts before reconciliation, run both unchanged release gates, then verify health from an independent clone and wait for CI."
  "2026-10-19T02:00:48.650Z",codex-agent,"Merge inspection: main is 68e7b89, and only CHANGELOG.md conflicted. Main's changelog was selected before canonical regeneration. No tracker conflicts or clone-local merge receipts were produced, so reconciliation is unnecessary. Local strict health has no integrity or drift failures; it reports the existing host extension version skew (pinned CLI 2026.10.13 versus installed extension host 2026.10.18). Independent clone health will verify the committed tracker without that host state."
  "2026-10-19T02:20:46.797Z",codex-agent,"The orchestrator added review thread PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM6tw-Qw before any push. Merge c0aba84 is already complete and clean; do not repeat it. Stop the two unfinished pre-refactor release gates and preserve their logs as superseded runs, then scan each PR body once into a declaration-ID set, add a many-item/many-PR result regression, and run both full unchanged gates on the combined change. Existing attribution tests remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-19T02:27:00.152Z",codex-agent,"PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM6tw-Qw: replace per-item RegExp construction/body scans with one whole-line scan per PR and set membership per item. Keep the original six attribution tests byte-for-byte unchanged. Focused suite: 7/7, zero skipped/cancelled/failed. New real-SDK bulk case: 40 items, 12 PRs, 24 deliveries, 2 ambiguous claimant rows and 12 mention-only rows; all stored statuses remain open in plan mode. The same new result test passes 1/1 against only the pre-refactor runCloseout implementation in the scratch clone: equivalence is required here, so this optimization control intentionally passes before and after and uses no timing assertion. Earlier correctness function-only revert proofs remain recorded above. Lint and docstring checks pass. Superseded gate runs were stopped on the orchestrator's interruption and are not completed gate evidence."
  "2026-10-19T02:29:22.294Z",codex-agent,"PM-linked verification completed: npx pm test pm-github-uqjf --run --progress passed both linked commands (attribution 7/7; compact same-repo dry-run control 1/1), zero timeouts/skips/failures. The project disables linked-result storage, so this comment is the durable receipt; no policy was changed. Canonical changelog regeneration and check pass after tracker writes. Commit the combined refactor and evidence before the two full release gates."
  "2026-10-19T03:03:25.411Z",codex-agent,"Combined-head gate progress at code head ed63b0e: repeated orchestrator pauses stopped unfinished gate processes; those logs are superseded, not acceptance receipts. The continuing npm run has passed the original watchdog and all seven attribution cases. The concurrent Bun invocation hit existing pm-github-sah1 at bounded-cli.test.ts:20: /ready/ assertion received empty stdout before the unchanged 500 ms startup deadline. Stop that already-failed attempt; later cancellations are stop consequences. The unchanged isolated watchdog suite passes 2/2. A full Bun rerun is queued to start automatically only after npm completes with exit 0. No source, threshold, helper, budget or dependency-pin changes were made in response."
  "2026-10-19T03:18:48.987Z",codex-agent,"Completed npm run release:check at code head ed63b0ef0fd2ea505d036144f3667beb6ad46b37: exit 0, 910/910 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips. Exact coverage over all 15 authored modules: 10506/10506 lines and statements, 275/275 functions, 3210/3210 branches; all four dimensions 100 percent with no source exemptions or threshold changes. Every remaining release-check stage passed. The full unchanged Bun rerun started automatically only after npm exited successfully."
  "2026-10-19T03:30:14.703Z",codex-agent,"Equivalence review found an edge case in the first Set implementation: JavaScript lowercasing maps the Unicode Kelvin sign to ASCII k, but the old non-Unicode /i regex rejects that lookalike. Correct the lookup key to preserve the original regex canonicalization, retaining per-PR scanning and Set membership. Extend the same 40-item/12-PR result test with a bulk-prefixed item's Kelvin-sign lookalike and non-ASCII expansion cases; the original six tests remain unchanged. The completed 910-test npm receipt belongs to ed63b0e only. Stop the unfinished Bun run as superseded by this correction; verify the old-function equivalence control and a key-function-only failing revert, then rerun both complete unchanged gates on the corrected code."
  "2026-10-19T03:31:39.404Z",codex-agent,"Strict case-equivalence proof completed: full attribution suite 7/7, zero failures/cancellations/skips; the six original tests remain byte-for-byte unchanged. Enhanced 40-item/12-PR bulk case passes 1/1 against the original runCloseout function. Reverting only declarationKey to ordinary lowercasing makes that same result test fail with ERR_ASSERTION (exit 1); restoring the key passes 1/1. This preserves the original non-Unicode /i behavior, including Kelvin-sign rejection, without per-item body scans or timing assertions. Lint passes; docstring gate documents all 171 declarations. Commit this correction and run fresh complete npm and Bun gates sequentially at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-19T03:53:51.087Z",codex-agent,"Completed corrected npm run release:check at 23495cf5469f0d0b6f5795b147a852dde4ca41fb: exit 0; 910/910 tests; zero failures, cancellations or skips. Exact 100/100/100/100 over all 15 authored modules: 10518/10518 lines and statements, 276/276 functions and 3216/3216 branches. All remaining release-check stages passed, including privacy, canonical changelog and attestation checks. Thresholds, source scope, helper/test budgets and pins are unchanged. The full corrected Bun gate has now started alone after npm's successful exit. This receipt supersedes the earlier code-head acceptance evidence for final review."
  "2026-10-19T04:26:24.846Z",codex-agent,"Completed BOTH corrected release gates at code head 23495cf5469f0d0b6f5795b147a852dde4ca41fb: npm run release:check exit 0 and bun run release:check exit 0. Each passed 910/910 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations, exact 100/100/100/100 over all 15 authored modules: 10518/10518 lines and statements, 276/276 functions, 3216/3216 branches. Every stage passed at unchanged thresholds, source scope, helper/test budgets and pins. Corrected PM-linked commands passed 2/2 (attribution 7/7, compact dry-run 1/1); result tracking remains disabled by existing policy, so these comments are the durable record. Original six tests are unchanged; old-function bulk control passes, key-function-only lowercase revert fails with ERR_ASSERTION, restored bulk test passes. Merge c0aba84 incorporated main 68e7b89 with only the changelog conflict resolved from main then regenerated; no clone-local receipts or pending reconciliation. The existing startup-watchdog follow-up remains open; the completed corrected Bun gate passed it unchanged. Prepare the final receipt, release the claim, and leave the item in_progress. Exact receipt-head fresh-clone health and CI results will be recorded in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/150 after the single push."
  "2026-10-20T14:09:10.532Z",codex-agent,"Continuing https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/issues/33 under the owner rule: recognize the structured PM item: declaration used by PR 19, reject incidental PM: lists and tracker PR metadata alone, and select the latest merged declaring PR whose checks pass. Preserve existing history. Add real non-git tracker regressions, consistent evidence readback and function-only revert proofs; run both unchanged release gates."
  "2026-10-20T14:13:47.034Z",codex-agent,"Implemented structured PM item: declarations and latest eligible merge selection before SDK writes. Tracker PR URL metadata alone no longer declares delivery. Real non-git scenarios use distinct revisions/check names and verify completed_at, resolution, actual_result, close_reason and the appended close patch. Historical function-only revert restores runCloseout from dc86e83: all three required regressions fail directly with ERR_ASSERTION, exit 1 (earlier gap wins; mention closes; prefix mention closes). Restoring origin/main functions separately fails the latest-selection regression; prefix-broadening mutation also fails directly. No test-load failure counts as proof. Typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication check pass."
  "2026-10-20T14:14:36.148Z",codex-agent,"All eight real-tracker attribution scenarios pass. The broader closeout run exposed only an existing assertion on the mention diagnostic; retained its phrase while adding Mentioned, not delivered. Linked tests initially refused commands inherited from a different branch; reviewed and acknowledged the existing commands for this clone, then reran without changing project trust or result-storage policies. Full npm and Bun gates will run sequentially with isolated git identity."
  "2026-10-20T14:15:44.467Z",codex-agent,"Linked pm test run passed both registered commands: attribution 8/8 and compact dry-run control 1/1, zero failures/skips/timeouts. Result storage is disabled by existing project policy; this comment is the durable receipt. The first full npm gate found a test-only TypeScript inference error in the per-PR fact table before coverage ran; corrected the annotation to Partial<Record<...>> and build:test passes. Full gates are being restarted on the corrected test source."
  "2026-10-20T14:16:37.445Z",codex-agent,"Final boundary review restricts structured PM item: links to a standalone line (plain or markdown), so follow-up prose such as leaves the item open remains not_delivery. Added its real non-git regression. Reverting only declaresDelivery to the first implementation makes this new negative regression fail directly with ERR_ASSERTION, exit 1. The original three historical-function revert proofs and latest-selection proof remain valid."
  "2026-10-20T14:46:47.924Z",codex-agent,"The complete npm coverage test run finished 958/960 with two expected-behavior assertions still tied to ambiguous_delivery: public compact output expected three rows instead of one selected delivery, and packed CLI expected zero closes instead of two. Updated those acceptance assertions to verify the winning PR, duplicate_selection counts, two applies and an idempotent repeat. The earlier direct closeout run had also reported these; they were missed when inspecting only its tail. No implementation, thresholds or test budgets changed. Running the complete closeout suite to completion before restarting both full gates."
  "2026-10-20T14:54:01.782Z",codex-agent,"Corrected complete closeout suite passed 99/99, zero failures/cancellations/skips. Focused c8 --100 run over closeout.ts also passed 99/99 with exact 100/100/100/100; the bare-link plus separate closing-ID declaration covers the required reference-upgrade boundary. Public compact output selects PR 44 and counts two duplicate selections; packed CLI closes two selected items and repeats with zero writes. Final linked pm test run passes attribution 9/9 and compact control 1/1. Failed full-run coverage was 99.94 percent because the old assertions stopped later code and the upgrade arm needed this positive case; thresholds and source scope remain unchanged. Restart both complete release gates sequentially on this committed test correction."
  "2026-10-20T15:40:09.444Z",codex-agent,"Completed npm run release:check at d8683ff37db274b8fcf569baf97f1c230514a12d with isolated git identity: exit 0; 960/960 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations; exact 100/100/100/100 over all 16 authored modules. Lines/statements 11037/11037, functions 299/299, branches 3511/3511. Every release-check stage passed at unchanged thresholds, inventory, dependency pins and test/helper budgets. The full bun run release:check has now started sequentially on the same code; its completion remains pending. Earlier failed runs are superseded by this completed npm receipt."
  "2026-10-20T16:51:30.127Z",codex-agent,"Completed BOTH full release gates at d8683ff37db274b8fcf569baf97f1c230514a12d: npm run release:check exit 0 and bun run release:check exit 0, sequentially with isolated git identity. Each passed 960/960 tests with zero failures/skips/cancellations and exact 100/100/100/100 across all 16 authored modules: lines/statements 11037/11037, functions 299/299, branches 3511/3511. Every stage passed, including typecheck, build, docstrings, lint, duplication, privacy, coverage, production audit, pack dry run, changelog and publish-attestation verification. Runtime source, tests, package pins, source inventory, exclusions, thresholds and helper/test budgets are unchanged between gates. Focused closeout 99/99 and linked pm tests 9/9 plus 1/1 pass. Three required historical-function revert regressions fail directly; main-function latest-selection revert and prefix/structured-prose controls also fail. Preparing the PR and final claim release; no merge, package release or pm-ado mutation."
  "2026-10-20T16:55:40.228Z",codex-agent,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/159 is open with the requested title and a mergeable head. Verified the published original body and head; an automatic public summary was appended without changing the submitted matcher table, regression proof or gate receipts. Source/test gate head remains d8683ff37db274b8fcf569baf97f1c230514a12d: npm and Bun release checks both pass 960/960 with exact 100/100/100/100 across 16 authored modules. Tracker validation returns ok true with metadata, linked-file and clone-local test-trust warnings; no new PM CLI/SDK defect was found. Remote CI/review is pending and no approval is claimed. Release the claim, keep the item in_progress, and hand off for orchestrator verification. No merge, package release or pm-ado write was performed."
  "2026-10-20T17:11:28.505Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR 159: fetched every review thread and comment (one unresolved thread, no additional comment pages), plus latest CodeRabbit review 5588689349 (no outside-diff findings). Verifying metadata-only versus body-reference reporting, correcting all equivalent documentation, adding regression and behavioral revert proof, then running unchanged npm and Bun release gates. Branch is current with main; no merge needed."
  "2026-10-20T17:12:55.334Z",codex-agent,"Verified thread PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM6ub0vv against runCloseout: candidate rows come only from canonical body references or standalone declarations, and eligibility checks precede not_delivery. Fixed README and the attribution evidence table. Full PR self-review found no further reporting-contract instances. Added a real non-git metadata-only fixture plus two documentation contract checks. Revert proof: restoring README alone from 9c08fc2 makes its new contract check fail ERR_ASSERTION (exit 1); restoring only the attribution doc does likewise. Restoring only runCloseout from origin/main makes the metadata-only fixture fail ERR_ASSERTION (closed 1 instead of 0, exit 1). Every reversion was restored afterward. No runtime fix was needed for this documentation finding."
  "2026-10-20T17:21:50.558Z",codex-agent,"Restored acceptance: pm test pm-github-uqjf --run --progress --timeout 600 passed both linked commands, attribution 12/12 and compact control 1/1 (zero failures/skips/cancellations). The default 120-second linked run timed out under host load; retry passed unchanged in 276 seconds. Restored documentation-only checks also pass 2/2. An exploratory full focused run overlapped the deliberate README revert and was discarded, not counted as acceptance. npm release gate has passed typecheck, build, docstrings, lint, duplication and privacy (6022 local objects), and is running full coverage. Bun gate follows sequentially."
  "2026-10-20T19:02:00.310Z",codex-agent,"Full npm release:check passed at code/test head 2fa4571247b5f86b984c588f32b494538a2f89ee with isolated git identity: 963/963 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips. All 16 authored modules meet exact 100/100/100/100: lines and statements 11037/11037, functions 299/299, branches 3510/3510. Every release stage passed at unchanged pins, source inventory, exclusions and thresholds. Sequential full Bun release validation starts next. Review refresh still contains only PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM6ub0vv with one comment, no pagination; latest CodeRabbit review remains 5588689349 with no outside-diff section."
  "2026-10-20T20:40:47.775Z",codex-agent,"Final review acceptance at code/test head 2fa4571247b5f86b984c588f32b494538a2f89ee: npm run release:check AND bun run release:check each exit 0, 963/963 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips, exact 100/100/100/100 across all 16 authored modules. Both count lines/statements 11037/11037, functions 299/299, branches 3510/3510. Every release stage passed sequentially with isolated git identity; pins, thresholds, inventory and exclusions are unchanged. Linked pm retry passed attribution 12/12 and compact control 1/1 with timeout 600; the default 120-second host-load timeout is superseded by the unchanged passing retry. New documentation reversions each fail ERR_ASSERTION, exit 1; runCloseout-only reversion to main 4e18c93 fails the new metadata-only fixture (closed 1 instead of 0). Corrected README and attribution table for PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM6ub0vv; full PR self-review found no additional instance. Only this thread remains in the refreshed review corpus; no outside-diff findings. No new PM CLI/SDK defect encountered. Final receipt changes contain only docs and append-only pm evidence, with runtime source/tests identical to the verified head. Release the claim and retain in_progress for orchestrator verification. No thread replies/resolutions, merge, release, or other repository edits."
